cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its study records, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Telohelm: replacing repeated language-model decisions with tested procedures"
abstract: >-
  Telohelm is a self-adaptive agent that replaces repeated language-model
  decisions with procedures that a reasoning model writes between episodes.
  A separate monitor admits a procedure only after replaying recorded
  episodes with it and no model calls, and the records show whether each
  adopted procedure acts later. The repository holds the agent, the
  simulated air-to-air refuelling task, the study runner, protocol
  and analysis, and the readers that reproduce the paper's tables, including
  a comparison with the reasoning model flying alone; the study records are
  archived with it on Zenodo.
